@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ export const APP_GUIDE = `TerraX is a browser-based Earth-observation workbench
 Tools:
 - Forest loss: two-date NDVI change (upload an earlier and a later GeoTIFF on the same grid; single-band NDVI or multi-band with red and NIR). Forest = NDVI ≥ threshold (default 0.5) on the earlier image; loss = ΔNDVI ≤ threshold (default −0.2); reports forest area, loss and gain in hectares and a change map. Also reads Hansen Global Forest Change "lossyear" tiles (optional "treecover2000", default canopy ≥ 30 %) and reports loss by year, and maps burn severity from pre/post NBR (dNBR, USGS FIREMON classes: low from 0.10, moderate-low 0.27, moderate-high 0.44, high 0.66). An optional minimum mapping unit (ha) removes smaller 8-connected patches; loss or burned patches export as GeoJSON polygons.
